    deferOrBlockReason:
      "Uncapped run persisted no recipes: the site answers the recipe API with a Cloudflare managed challenge (HTTP 403, cf-mitigated: challenge). A plain client cannot clear it, and neither can the hardened browser path from this host, so the route needs a request identity this project does not have rather than a crawler fix\n\nThe challenge is gone as of 2026-09-18, and nothing here was changed to achieve that - the site's own mitigation was lifted. /wp-json/wp/v2/wprm_recipe?per_page=100&page=1 answers HTTP 200 through the same Cloudflare edge with 982 KB of JSON and no cf-mitigated header, and the paging headers read x-wp-total 651 over x-wp-totalpages 7. The first record parses as a real WPRM recipe, Cashewnoeddemaelk med vanilje, carrying its ingredients and instructions.\n\nShadow comparison passed on 2026-09-18, hours after that probe, and the run replaces it as the evidence. The uncapped run 2026-09-18T19-09-35 walked 651 candidates and persisted 648 with discovery complete, 0 failed and 0 blocked; the 3 it declined are 2 the contract reads as incomplete and 1 whose WPRM payload is malformed, and 648 + 2 + 1 is 651 exactly. The repeat, 2026-09-18T19-11-30, was STABLE with 648 of 648 byte-identical.\n\nThe isolated legacy run emitted 650. Every one of V2's 648 is among them, V2 holds nothing legacy lacks, and every material field matches on all 648. The 2 legacy holds alone are precisely the 2 the completeness contract refuses - records legacy accepts without a name, ingredients or instructions - and the 1 malformed record is held by neither side. The comparator noted only intentional differences: 4 records keep WPRM named-step prefixes legacy drops, and 4 keep a space at a block boundary legacy fuses over.\n\nNine stored records were checked through impit against the live page: 9 of 9 matched in full, title, every ingredient and every step. The negative control failed as it should. A store scan found none of the four shared WPRM text defects - 0 raw shortcodes, 0 entity-escaped titles, 0 doubly-parenthesised notes.\n\nOne characteristic is recorded rather than tidied away. 37 of the 648 records carry a canonical of the form /?p=NNNN&post_type=wprm_recipe rather than a slug, and 36 of those 37 share a title with a slug record, so the source publishes them twice. That is not a V2 artefact: the isolated legacy capture contains the same 37 ?p= URLs, which is why the comparison finds nothing only one side holds. Both implementations reproduce the source's own duplication faithfully, and de-duplicating it would be a change of behaviour rather than a fix.",
