    "Depth-first bounded canary persisted seven recipes without operational failures and every material field matched the legacy parser on those exact pages; Crawlee uses final numeric request URLs to avoid the site's stale cross-recipe canonical collisions, while the roughly 39000-recipe hierarchy remains unvalidated.\n\nThat hierarchy is now measured against the clock rather than guessed at. An uncapped run started 2026-09-09 and was killed by its 24-hour ceiling with 25245 recipes in the store and no run summary written, which is the second time this source has been cut off - the first was at 43200s. The rate is not the problem and neither is the ceiling arithmetic: 25245 records in 24 hours is about 1050 an hour, or 3.4 seconds each, which is exactly what a delay of 3 seconds at a concurrency of 1 produces. Reaching 39000 therefore takes something near 37 hours before listing and category pages are counted at all.\n\nThe pacing is not a knob to turn here. Legacy\'s own spider sets DOWNLOAD_DELAY 3 and CONCURRENT_REQUESTS_PER_DOMAIN 1 in its custom_settings, well below the project defaults of 2 and 2, so its author chose to be gentle with this site deliberately and V2 matches that choice exactly. Crawling faster would both diverge from the reference and risk a site nobody has seen refuse us. Re-queued at a 216000s ceiling instead. The records already in the store are not lost - upserts had already landed - but a run that is killed writes no summary, so it can prove nothing about completeness.\n\nThe 216000s run finished on its own on 2026-09-12 after about 46.5 hours, inside the ceiling for the first time in three attempts. It persisted 39184 recipes over 50213 requests with discovery complete, no page cap, no failed request and no blocked request, and refused 41 pages as incomplete; 39184 stored plus 41 refused is exactly the 39225 recipe pages processed. The store holds 39184 distinct URLs from this run, plus one document left from an earlier one.\n\nThe run reports 597904 discovered candidates, and that is not a gap of more than half a million. The counter is incremented with every recipe link a listing page yields before de-duplication, and this site links the same recipe from many places in its category hierarchy; the crawler admits each canonical URL once, which is where 39225 comes from. It is the figure to read, and it agrees with the roughly 39000 recipes the hierarchy was estimated at.\n\nAn isolated legacy comparison comes next and will be long: legacy crawls this site at the same 3 seconds and one request in flight.\n\nThe isolated legacy comparison finished on 2026-09-15 after about 51 hours, with scrapy exit 0. Legacy emitted 39227 records and V2 holds 39184 from run 2026-09-10. Nothing is V2-only. Of the 43 only legacy holds, 41 are records without a name, ingredients or instructions that legacy accepts and V2 refuses, which matches the 41 incomplete pages this run refused. The other 2 are complete. One is /opskrifter/41260/bmo-bolle-med-ost, one id past the highest V2 stored, 41259, so it was published after the V2 run. The other, /opskrifter/25532/mere-svinekam-boulangere, is an old id that V2 holds under no URL; it extracts completely today and is not yet explained. Two records differ on a field, both on abrikostrifli: V2 stored 150 g. Bisca KarenVolf makroner and a longer first step, while legacy and the live page today read 150 g. makroner and the shorter step. The page was edited between the V2 fetch on 2026-09-11 and the legacy fetch. That is 39182 of 39184 shared records matching on every material field, and the only difference is an upstream edit. It is not promoted yet, for two reasons: this run has no repeat, and 25532 is open. A repeat at the same 3-second pacing was queued at 2026-09-15T00:10 and takes about two days; it will also show whether discovery now reaches 25532.\n\nThe repeat finished on 2026-09-17 after about 56 hours and was clean: 0 failed, 0 blocked, discovery complete, 39185 persisted and 41 pages refused as incomplete. Against the previous run it reported STABLE, 39180 of 39187 stored records identical, 5 edited upstream and 2 added by the site. Re-compared against the same legacy run: legacy 39227, V2 39185, 43 only legacy and 1 only V2. Of the 43, 41 are the incomplete pages V2 refuses. One is /opskrifter/18042/champignon-i-hvidloeg, which is not missing at all: the site renamed the slug, and the single V2-only record is the same recipe at champignon-i-hvidloeg-champinones-al-ajillo. That leaves exactly one recipe V2 does not hold, /opskrifter/25532/mere-svinekam-boulangere, and the earlier note that it was unexplained can now be replaced. The page answers 200 and extracts completely, but it is orphaned from the hierarchy both crawlers walk: it carries no category or breadcrumb link, and the category page it would belong under lists no recipes today. The sitemap named in robots.txt, /sitemap/sitemap.xml, cannot close the gap either - its ten nested files hold 1040 URLs and not one recipe address. /opskrifter/41260, open in the earlier note, is now stored. Three ingredient lists and three step lists differ. Two are upstream edits, makrontaerte-med-kanelfloede and landskronataerte, where the stored record matches the live page exactly today and legacy holds the older text. The third is this source known defect rather than an extraction fault: /opskrifter/5339/guiso is stored with the title GUISO and another recipe ingredients, three toast items, while the page today carries one Recipe scope with the beef and potato ingredients legacy also saw. The site served a mismatched body under that numeric URL during the run. Held at canary_passed: the shadow gate asks that V2 hold every complete recipe legacy holds, and 25532 is one it does not.",
