    latestCanary: "2026-08-19T17-34-06.299Z",
    deferOrBlockReason:
      "Uncapped run persisted 1080 recipes with discovery complete and no failed requests, replacing a bounded 50-request probe. The legacy comparison is characterised but not settled. Legacy holds 1081 records to V2's 1080 and reads no instructions at all on any of them while V2 keeps the real steps; that is legacy discarding what V2 keeps, and the comparison now allows it. What remains is ingredients on 216 records, splitting two ways. On 200 the sides hold the same distinct ingredients and differ only in repeat counts - legacy lists an entry twice where the source's JSON-LD lists it once, so V2 is the faithful side. On the other 15 the source itself splits an ingredient across two entries - tuna-melt states '4 tsk.' and 'BBQ-sovs' separately - and legacy rejoins them while V2 stores what the page says. Joining a dangling quantity to the entry after it would be an improvement, but it changes ingredient output for every source and 842 promoted sources rest on the current output, so that belongs in a deliberate corpus-wide change rather than one source's promotion. Characterised 2026-08-31. This family has one member, so the state here is gocook's alone.\n\nThat dangling-quantity problem turned out to be ours after all, and it is fixed. The comparison ran three times against three successive stores and the ingredient differences went 226 records, then 14, then 4. The first drop came from no longer collapsing an ingredient list through a Set - gocook states salt twice, once per component, and 197 of its records lost an entry to that. The second came from not splitting an entry at a full stop belonging to a measure, which is what turned the published 4 tsk. BBQ-sovs into two entries.\n\nThe last 4 were the same defect wearing different words: Evt. Krymmel and 1 dl chokoladeknapper, f.eks. Smarties. Neither full stop ends a sentence. Running the current extractor over a freshly fetched /opskrift/kanelkage on 2026-09-10 returns 10 ingredients ending in a single entry reading Evt. Krymmel, which is exactly what legacy holds, so the fix is confirmed on live markup rather than on a fixture.\n\nThe fourth comparison, 2026-09-11, against a store carrying that fix leaves one ingredient difference in 1080 records, and it is V2 that is wrong. gocook publishes Fuldkornsbroed. Se efter noeglehulsmaerket og/eller fuldkornsmaerket. as a single entry - an ingredient followed by a note - and the splitter divides it at what really is a sentence boundary. The splitter earns its place on sources that pack several ingredients into one string, so one record is not enough to change it; recorded instead. The progression across four comparisons is 226 records, 14, 4, 1.\n\nWhat remains beside it: 3 prep and 1 total, on pages that publish PT0M for every time field so that both crawlers fall back to guessing from rendered text and disagree; and the tags column, where legacy is the broken side - its tags for this source hold the whole page as prose rather than any tag. The record sets are 1080 against legacy 1081, with no crawlee-only records and one legacy-only that the completeness contract refuses.\n\nThat account of the time differences was wrong and the repeat gate found out why: V2 was not guessing from rendered text, it was reading another recipe. gocook fills its own times in client-side, so the page reads Samlet tid: Arbejdstid: Svaerhedsgrad: Nem with nothing between the labels while related-recipe cards further down carry theirs as text. Scanning every candidate for the first parseable duration picked up a neighbour, and which neighbour depended on where the carousel sat: the repeat came back CHANGED with 1076 of 1080 identical and all four that moved differed only on times, 60 to 180, 330 to 30, 145 to 25 and 150 to 210 across two runs of the same pages. Counting only the first occurrence of a label, and only the text between it and the next labelled field, leaves times on 1079 of 1080 records and makes the repeat STABLE at 1080 to 1080 with all 1080 identical.\n\nThe fifth comparison, 2026-09-11, closes the source. Legacy finished on its own terms - 1082 requests, every one HTTP 200, no error logged - and emitted 1081 records in 44 minutes, with no crawlee-only records and one legacy-only, malede-aeg, that the completeness contract refuses. Four classes of field difference remain, each attributed. The tags column differs on all 1080 because legacy holds the whole page there as prose rather than any tag. 8 prep times and 1 total are cases where legacy carries a number and V2 carries none, and V2 is the correct side: legacy parses the first duration in whichever blob mentions arbejdstid, the same defect just fixed here, and it is no more stable - it reported 25 minutes for kyllingelaar-med-cornflakes in one run and 120 in the next, for a page that publishes no prep time at all. The last is one ingredient in 1080 where V2 is wrong, the Fuldkornsbroed entry split at a real sentence boundary, and one record does not justify changing behaviour many sources rely on.",
